      "biography": "Mojave 3 were a British rock band formed in the wake of Slowdive’s breakup in 1995, bringing together Neil Halstead, Rachel Goswell, and Ian McCutcheon before later adding keyboardist Alan Forrester and guitarist Simon Rowe. The group emerged from the shoegaze world but quickly moved toward a softer, more atmospheric style shaped by dream pop, slowcore, folk, and acoustic textures.\n\nTheir debut album, Ask Me Tomorrow, arrived in 1996 on 4AD and set the tone for a run of records that included Out of Tune, Excuses for Travellers, Spoon and Rafter, and Puzzles Like You. Mojave 3 became known for their restrained, melancholy songwriting and their ability to translate the emotional haze of shoegaze into a more spacious, roots-leaning sound, earning a loyal following and critical respect for their subtle evolution.\n\nAfter releasing five albums, the band went on hiatus in 2007, returned for live dates in 2011, and later effectively ended when Halstead and Goswell reformed Slowdive.",
