    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Excuses for Travellers is Mojave 3’s third studio album, released by 4AD in 2000, and it finds the band refining the hushed, melancholic sound that had defined their earlier work. Built around Neil Halstead’s understated songwriting and gentle vocals, the album blends dream pop, indie rock, and acoustic textures into a warm, introspective record that feels both intimate and carefully layered.\n\nThe songs move with a slow, spacious grace, drawing on pedal steel, horns, piano, and subtle electronic touches from producer Mark Van Hoen to deepen the mood without overwhelming it. Highlights such as “In Love with a View,” “Any Day Will Be Fine,” and “Return to Sender” helped make it one of Mojave 3’s most admired releases, and it was received positively by critics, with a Metacritic average of 77.",
